From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:59:38 +0200
Subject: [scopes] Mark saved class variable as MaybeAssigned
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When a class has static private methods or accessors that require
runtime brand checks (should_save_class_variable()), its class_variable
is context-allocated and loaded with HoleCheckMode::kElided during
static brand checks (obj.#x or #x in obj). Because the hole check is
elided, no ThrowReferenceErrorIfHole is emitted when loading
class_variable before the class constructor finishes initializing.

If class_variable is marked kNotAssigned in ScopeInfo, Maglev caches
uninitialized loads (which evaluate to the_hole) in
loaded_context_constants_ and reuses the stale the_hole value even after
class evaluation finishes and stores the constructor into the context.

Mark class_variable as kMaybeAssigned in ScopeInfo whenever
should_save_class_variable() is true so that loads are treated as
mutable context slot accesses across all tiers and lazy compilation
without needing bytecode overrides.

Bug: 559932543
TAG=agy
CONV=1b7d9654-2731-4157-8abc-cd9414138332

Change-Id: I84e6ef2f096ad1999591366df1f70c397f14aca2
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8425123
Reviewed-by: Marja Hölttä <marja@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#110032}

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y): the ClassScope constructor on V8 14.8
still passes kNoSourcePosition for the saved class variable (the
access-position plumbing is not on this branch); only the
set_maybe_assigned() call is added there.

